    <DataNode elementId="AT3G26830-MONOMER" textLabel="Bifunctional dihydrocamalexate synthase/camalexin synthase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9LW27" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="635" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">CYP71B15 catalyzes the final step in camalexin biosynthesis. Its expression is induced locally upon infection by camalexin-inducing pathogens. CYP71B15 is a novel plant enzyme in that it is the only known cytochrome P450 in plants results in simultaneous decarboxylation and introduction of a C-C double bond.</Comment>
